<p>If your printer supports an ink saving function, the following describes 
 how you can save on ink.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Ink Save:</span> 
 list, select <span class="Term-Soft">On</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
